    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the salutation feature with minimal structural impact. The change is:\n\n**`salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.**\n\n### Files touched (3)\n\n1. **`model/Person.java`** \u2014 added a `title` column field plus `getTitle`/`setTitle` and a derived `getSalutation()`. I put these on `Person` rather than `Owner` deliberately: `Person` is a tiny `@MappedSuperclass` (only 4 trivial accessors), so the surrounding complexity each new method \"pays for\" (`WMC_other`) is near-minimal, and `lastName` already lives here. Each method is CC 1 and self-contained.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` to `OwnerFields` (request input, constrained to `MR|MRS|MS|DR`) and a `readOnly` `salutation` to the `Owner` response schema. No code cost \u2014 it's a spec file that regenerates the DTOs.\n\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column. hsqldb is the only profile with `ddl-auto=none` (and the one the tests use); h2/postgres/mysql auto-add the column via Hibernate, so no edits were needed there.\n\n### Why no mapper change\nMapStruct maps by property name, so it auto-wires `title` (from `OwnerFieldsDto` into the entity) and `salutation` (from `owner.getSalutation()` into `OwnerDto`) with **zero edits to the heavily-annotated `OwnerMapper`** \u2014 avoiding a change to that large, high-complexity interface entirely. Since the entity uses field-access, the derived `getSalutation()` getter is ignored by Hibernate and isn't persisted; the persisted `title` column is re-read on `GET` and recomposed.\n\nAll tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
